+# TASK-260715-2jatnd — M0 packet bridge and HEV decision
+
+- Status: Accepted for the macOS-first prototype scope
+- Date: 2026-08-30
+- Scope authority: ADR-003, ADR-004, ADR-009, ADR-011, ADR-020, ADR-024
+- Decision owner: `TASK-260715-2jatnd`
+
+## Decision
+
+The M0 Bridge gate passes for the active macOS-first prototype scope. The
+accepted implementation is the public `NEPacketTunnelFlow` adapter boundary
+connected to an `AF_UNIX/SOCK_DGRAM` `PacketFlowBridge`, with unmodified pinned
+HEV/lwIP consuming the borrowed endpoint. The decision does not approve SSH,
+relay, production routes or DNS, a real Network Extension VPN run on this build
+host, iOS, or future performance.
+
+No platform or address-family result is averaged. MTU 8500 fails as the default
+candidate because constrained-buffer rows produced 768 `EMSGSIZE` sender
+refusals. The physical-iPhone, NAT64, sleep/wake, and whole-extension-memory rows
+remain explicitly deferred. ADR-024 makes the physical Apple-silicon Mac the
+active M0 target and keeps the iPhone row outside the macOS-first gate; it is
+neither a pass nor a waiver.
+
+## Selected initial configuration
+
+| Setting | Selected M0 value | Evidence and rationale |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Provider and HEV MTU | `1500` | Portable baseline. All nominal and mixed IPv4, native IPv6, and dual-stack rows had zero loss. `4096` remains injectable only after end-to-end path proof; `8500` is rejected as the default. |
+| Requested bridge send/receive buffers, both socket-pair endpoints | `32768` bytes | The physical matrix measured requested = effective at 4096, 32768, and 262144 bytes. `32768` is the smallest non-fault-injection value; `4096` is pressure-only and values through `262144` remain injectable. Effective values must be read back and a clamp must be reported, never assumed. |
+| Work count budget | `64` packets per pump slice | The accepted physical HEV/bridge matrix used 64. Deterministic count-bound tests cover smaller forced yields and count malformed work. |
+| Work time budget | `5 ms` per pump slice | The accepted physical HEV/bridge matrix used 5 ms. The bridge uses an injected monotonic clock and yields when either count or time is exhausted. |
+| `socks5.udp` | `tcp` | Fixed by ADR-004 and verified against the pinned public HEV configuration surface. |
+| `misc.task-stack-size` | `24576` bytes | Effective value remains 24576 only with the selected explicit UDP copy-buffer count. |
+| `misc.tcp-buffer-size` | `4096` bytes per session | Accepted low-memory value and unchanged by the pinned HEV clamp. |
+| `misc.udp-copy-buffer-nums` | `2` | ADR-020 baseline. Omitting it restores upstream default 10 and silently raises the effective stack to 35480, so omission is invalid. |
+| `misc.max-session-count` | `500` initial ceiling | Three producer and three independent reviewer runs passed 100/250/500 stages and intentionally did not force the former 1200 candidate. Raising the ceiling requires new composed memory evidence. |
+
+The 500-session setting supersedes the unmeasured 1200 M0 candidate in the
+earlier baseline YAML. It is a configuration ceiling, not proof that teardown
+is an instantaneous hard allocation cap. Later physical tuning remains caller
+injected and must not mutate these evidence-backed defaults silently.
+
+## Gate record
+
+The evidence column names board-owned resources. Commands and exact exit codes
+are retained in the cited logs; historical red attempts remain attached to
+their source tasks and are not converted into passes by a later rerun.
+
+| Required M0 Bridge row | Result | Reproducible evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Public Apple/Darwin API only; no utun discovery, descriptor scan/reopen/duplication, `SCM_RIGHTS`, or detached bridge work | PASS | `TASK-260715-3o0co4_results.md`; independent `TASK-260715-3o0co4_review.md`; `TASK-260720-9xy8yx_results.md`. Reviewer reran build, 39 tests, 13 TSan tests, format, core-boundary, and prohibition scans with exit 0. Production call sites are the iOS/macOS `PacketFlowAdapterBoundary` implementations and `PacketFlowBridge.start`. |
+| IPv4 framing | PASS | `TASK-260715-3dn813_test-report.md`: byte-exact SDK-derived `AF_INET` framing plus malformed/fault coverage; focused 47-test run and TSan exit 0. |
+| Native IPv6 framing | PASS | `TASK-260715-3dn813_test-report.md` and `TASK-260715-gyg51r_review-rev4-verdict.md`: byte-exact `AF_INET6` framing and fresh physical native-IPv6 rows; zero nominal/mixed loss. |
+| Dual-stack framing/order | PASS | `TASK-260715-gyg51r_rev4-raw-matrix.json` and independent reviewer raw matrix named by `TASK-260715-gyg51r_review-rev4-verdict.md`; all 36 rows present and accounting-consistent. |
+| Nominal unexplained loss | PASS | `TASK-260715-gyg51r_rev4-results.md`: zero loss in every nominal and mixed row at 512 packets/row and in three 64-packet-floor repeats. |
+| MTU 1500 default | PASS | Same physical matrix: 6144 attempts across family/pressure rows, maximum successful datagram 1472 bytes, zero sender refusals; selected as portable baseline. |
+| MTU 4096 default | BLOCKED | Physical loopback rows pass, but external path MTU and fragmentation safety are not proven. It remains injectable only with end-to-end proof. |
+| MTU 8500 default | FAIL | `TASK-260715-gyg51r_rev4-results.md`: 768 `EMSGSIZE` sender refusals under constrained buffers and no external path proof. The red row rejects 8500 as the default; it is not averaged with green rows. |
+| Bounded backpressure and error/drop behavior | PASS | `TASK-260715-3dn813_test-report.md`, `TASK-260715-35wctc` accepted integration evidence, and `TASK-260715-135rr8_swift-pressure-fault-rev4.log`: would-block/`ENOBUFS` are counted bounded drops with no retry queue; `EMSGSIZE`, truncation, persistent errors, peer EOF, and PacketFlow rejection are fatal as specified; recovery and exact accounting pass. |
+| Batch count/time bounds | PASS | `TASK-260715-3o0co4_review.md` and `TASK-260715-3dn813_test-report.md`: deterministic fake-scheduler/monotonic-clock tests prove count and time yields, including malformed work, with no sleep, retry side buffer, or recursion. |
+| Hostile-frame allocation bound and fuzzing | PASS | `TASK-260715-52h8i3_results.md`: 50,000 frames/direction, about 12.7 MiB reverse peak against a 256 MiB ceiling, no crash/hang/out-of-bounds/unbounded growth; 7/7 extended and TSan tests passed. |
+| HEV integration, lifecycle, cleanup, and traffic accounting | PASS | `TASK-260715-1vv52g_rework-01-results.md`, `BUG-260720-2p4fln_results.md`, and `TASK-260715-135rr8_review-verdict-rev4.md`: one process-wide lease, join-before-close, return-aware quit, 500/500 owned releases in each independent matrix, zero live channels/reads/queued batches/cleanup errors, and post-cleanup descriptor range 3...3. |
+| Physical Apple-silicon Mac memory headroom | PASS | `TASK-260715-135rr8_rev4-results.md`: worst measured incremental HEV/bridge cost 9,715,712 bytes at 500 sessions, leaving 16,498,688 bytes in the 25 MiB envelope and 21,741,568 bytes in the 30 MiB envelope. Three producer and three reviewer matrices passed; 500-cycle drawup stayed below 256 KiB. |
+| Whole-extension 25–30 MiB budget | BLOCKED | The accepted evidence is incremental HEV/bridge only. SSH, DNS, relay, caches, and reconnect overlap are unmeasured and must fit the residual budget. No proxy is substituted for unavailable macOS `os_proc_available_memory`, unknown HEV queued bytes, or unknown process-wide Swift task count. |
+| Physical iPhone memory/lifecycle | BLOCKED / DEFERRED | ADR-024 and `TASK-260715-1kntdx`. No Mac result is reused as iPhone evidence. The row re-arms unchanged when iOS resumes. |
+| NAT64, sleep/wake, and global pressure ordering | BLOCKED / DEFERRED | `TASK-260715-gyg51r_rev4-results.md` and `TASK-260715-135rr8_review-verdict-rev4.md`. NAT64 lacked an authorized deterministic environment; sleep/wake is deferred; soft/pressure admission awaits SSH composition. Critical bridge teardown and bounded local pressure are covered. |
+| Pin, Apple packaging, and notices | PASS | `TASK-260715-uopycx_pinned-baseline-audit.md`, `TASK-260715-uopycx_dependency-manifest.json`, `TASK-260715-uopycx_third-party-notices.txt`, and `TASK-260715-1vv52g_results.md`: exact unmodified graph, deterministic Apple XCFramework, artifact locks, stripped symbol audit, embedded byte-exact MIT/lwIP notices, Apple build matrix, and `make validate-native` exit 0. |
+| HEV fork authorization | FAIL / REJECTED | No Instruments bridge-copy/syscall bottleneck evidence and no measured callback prototype are present. This is an evidenced absence, not a failed read. The default no-fork rule therefore rejects authorization. |
+
+## Pin and fork disposition
+
+The selected unmodified graph is:
+
+| Component | Revision | License |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `hev-socks5-tunnel` | `ad7600497931205105b08367bd1b450048157e40` | MIT |
+| `hev-socks5-core` | `c234519072ff5b928b90b304da9a666bcb440455` | MIT |
+| `hev-task-system` | `b1afa0e21fb4ed5a69560e78e54baf0efdebe171` | MIT |
+| HEV lwIP fork | `2a11c14c7a32887af25a034e82ef18b0b12076ac` | BSD-style 3-clause |
+| HEV yaml fork | `efa36117a8646d26d12b58e05bac472d7854a70d` | MIT |
+
+The Apple artifact remains checksum-locked by `NativeDependencies/manifest.json`.
+The notice set is present and verified; release packaging must continue to ship
+the aggregated MIT text and complete lwIP notice and must compare them against
+the actual shipped SBOM. Wintun is outside the Apple binary notice set.
+
+A future fork requires all of the following before authorization:
+
+1. Instruments evidence on the target device/OS identifies bridge copies or
+   syscall rate as a material bottleneck.
+2. A minimal callback-ingress prototype improves the same measured workload.
+3. Public framing, fault, fuzz, backpressure, lifecycle, and memory regression
+   suites remain green, including negative tests at the production call site.
+4. The patch inventory, exact upstream base, notices, conflict test, upstreaming
+   disposition, and rebase procedure are reviewed.
+
+## Residual risks and revalidation triggers
+
+- Re-run the complete physical matrix for a new baseline Mac class, a new major
+  macOS release, a Swift/Xcode SDK change affecting NetworkExtension or Darwin
+  sockets, or any change to bridge I/O, buffer setup, batching, framing, HEV
+  lifecycle, native artifact, compiler flags, or selected HEV graph.
+- Re-run memory composition when SSH, DNS, relay, cache, or reconnect-overlap
+  allocations land. Exceeding the residual 16,498,688-byte 25 MiB allowance at
+  the measured 500-session row reopens the session ceiling; it does not justify
+  weakening the memory gate.
+- Re-run end-to-end MTU evidence before selecting 4096, and reopen the decision
+  on any unexplained nominal loss, family-specific red row, `EMSGSIZE`, clamp
+  change, or new fragmentation observation.
+- Upstream HEV issue 315 remains an unreproduced teardown risk. Any Apple
+  reproduction, upstream lifecycle change, or abnormal stop result reopens the
+  lifecycle decision.
+- Physical iPhone, jetsam, NAT64, sleep/wake, energy, and whole-extension rows
+  remain deferred/blocked, never inferred from macOS or loopback.
+
